# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Product copy of Crux's clang-tidy selection. The check list equals Crux's, and a test compares
# the two. Only the header filter differs. Copy this file to the product root.
#
# Edit the header filter before use: replace <PRODUCT_ROOT> with the absolute path of the product
# repository, with any regex metacharacter in it escaped (for example /work/product). clang-tidy
# searches a header's full path with this regex, and a Zephyr compile database names headers by
# absolute path. Anchored to the root, the filter reports headers under app/, domain/, drivers/,
# include/ and tests/ of the product only, and not those of Zephyr, Crux, the SDK or a build
# directory, whose paths also contain include/, drivers/ or tests/. Left unedited, it matches no
# header, so only the source files themselves are reported. A path that differs per checkout can be
# passed instead on the command line, which overrides this file:
#   clang-tidy -p build --header-filter="^$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/(app|domain|drivers|include|tests)/" ...
#
# clang-tidy needs a compile database. A Zephyr build writes compile_commands.json when
# CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS is on. Crux does not provide one for a product, and nobody has run
# these checks on Zephyr driver sources here, so expect to tune the list for them.
# readability-identifier-naming has no options, so it reports nothing, as in Crux's own file: the
# naming rules of docs/coding-guidelines.md are not enforced by this file.
#
# Keep the C17 enum ABI and explicitly length-checked C library calls; these two
# generic checks flag the language/library form rather than a project defect.
Checks: >-
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  performance-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  portability-*,
  readability-identifier-naming
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '^<PRODUCT_ROOT>/(app|domain|drivers|include|tests)/'
FormatStyle: file
